# Cloudflare `_redirects` — parsed by the static-asset layer, never served.
#
# The playground uses `html_handling: "none"` (exact-path lookup) so that
# /embed.html stays a LITERAL 200, as it was on Vercel: it is a published URL,
# pasted into third-party <iframe> snippets, and a 307 to /embed would add a
# round trip to every embed on the internet for no gain.
#
# The cost of "none" is that `/` is not itself a file and would fall through to
# not_found_handling. A status-200 rule is a REWRITE, not a redirect, and the
# redirect layer runs before the asset lookup — so this serves index.html at the
# site root with no redirect and no 404.
/    /index.html    200

# Same mechanism, same reason, for the static example index that
# `scripts/gen-static.mjs` writes to dist/examples/index.html. With exact-path
# lookup a directory URL is not a file, so `/examples/` would 404 — and that URL
# is the one the playground's intro band, every example page's breadcrumb and the
# sitemap all point at. The 27 example pages themselves need no rule: they are
# real files at their own `.html` paths, which is why the canonical links and the
# sitemap entries carry the extension.
/examples/    /examples/index.html    200
